# delivery-fleet-rln — a fleet of validating relays, and two endpoints talking
# across it for as long as you ask.
#
# Three containerised relays, each holding its OWN membership and validating
# every proof it forwards, plus two host endpoints that meet only at the fleet
# and never dial each other. That last part is the topology's whole point: a
# message reaches the receiver only if a relay validated it, so the fleet is
# on the critical path rather than beside it.
#
# It needs the relay image, which carries published RLN modules:
#     bash tools/build-e2e-image.sh
NODES=5
NEEDS_MODULES="liblogos_lez_rln_module liblogos_rln_module delivery_module"
TARGETS="local"
RUNNER=bash
